# Vercel Web Design & Engineering Standards

> Build like Vercel ships: fast, accessible, beautiful, minimal cognitive load.
> Every millisecond counts. Every unnecessary element is noise.

## Performance Standards

### Core Web Vitals Targets
| Metric | Target | Max Acceptable |
|--------|--------|----------------|
| LCP (Largest Contentful Paint) | < 1.5s | < 2.5s |
| FID / INP (Interaction to Next Paint) | < 100ms | < 200ms |
| CLS (Cumulative Layout Shift) | < 0.05 | < 0.1 |
| TTFB (Time to First Byte) | < 200ms | < 600ms |

### Mandatory Optimizations
1. **Images**: Always use `next/image` with `width`, `height`, and appropriate `sizes` prop. Never use raw `<img>` tags.
   ```tsx
   // ✅ Correct
   <Image src="/hero.webp" alt="Descriptive alt" width={800} height={600} priority />
   
   // ❌ FORBIDDEN
   <img src="/hero.png" />
   ```

2. **Fonts**: Load via `next/font` for zero-CLS, self-hosted fonts. Never use `<link>` to Google Fonts CDN.
   ```tsx
   // ✅ Correct
   import { Inter } from 'next/font/google';
   const inter = Inter({ subsets: ['latin'], display: 'swap' });
   ```

3. **Code Splitting**: Use `dynamic()` for heavy components not needed on initial paint.
   ```tsx
   import dynamic from 'next/dynamic';
   const Chart = dynamic(() => import('@/components/ProgressChart'), {
     loading: () => <ChartSkeleton />,
     ssr: false,
   });
   ```

4. **Bundle Size**: Never import entire libraries when tree-shaking is available.
   ```tsx
   // ✅ Correct
   import { Chart as ChartJS, ArcElement } from 'chart.js';
   
   // ❌ FORBIDDEN
   import Chart from 'chart.js/auto';
   ```

5. **Server Components by Default**: Every component is a Server Component unless it explicitly needs client interactivity. Mark client components with `'use client'` only at the boundary.

6. **Streaming & Suspense**: Wrap slow data fetches in `<Suspense>` with meaningful fallbacks.

### What NOT To Ship
- ❌ `console.log` in production code
- ❌ Unused imports or dead code
- ❌ `any` type in TypeScript (use `unknown` + type guards instead)
- ❌ Inline styles (use Tailwind or CSS modules)
- ❌ `!important` in CSS (refactor specificity instead)
- ❌ `setTimeout` for animation timing (use CSS transitions or `requestAnimationFrame`)
- ❌ Synchronous `localStorage` reads in render path (causes hydration mismatches)

## Accessibility Standards (a11y)

### WCAG 2.1 AA Compliance — MANDATORY
1. **Color Contrast**: 
   - Normal text: ≥ 4.5:1 contrast ratio against background
   - Large text (≥18px bold or ≥24px): ≥ 3:1
   - UI components and graphical objects: ≥ 3:1
   - Use tools: WebAIM Contrast Checker, axe DevTools

2. **Keyboard Navigation**:
   - All interactive elements must be reachable via `Tab` key
   - Focus order must follow logical reading order
   - Custom components must implement proper `role`, `tabIndex`, `aria-*` attributes
   - **Focus trapping** in modals/dialogs — focus must not escape to background content
   - `Escape` key must close modals, dropdowns, and overlays

3. **Semantic HTML**:
   ```tsx
   // ✅ Correct
   <nav aria-label="Main navigation">
   <main>
   <section aria-labelledby="section-title">
   <button type="button" onClick={handleClick}>
   
   // ❌ FORBIDDEN
   <div onClick={handleClick}>  // div is not a button
   <div class="nav">            // div is not nav
   ```

4. **ARIA When Needed**:
   - Use native HTML elements FIRST (`<button>`, `<dialog>`, `<details>`)
   - Add `aria-label` for icon-only buttons
   - Use `aria-live="polite"` for dynamic content updates (toasts, counters)
   - Use `aria-expanded` for toggleable sections
   - Use `role="status"` for loading indicators

5. **Screen Reader Audit**:
   - Every image has meaningful `alt` text (or `alt=""` for decorative)
   - Form inputs have associated `<label>` elements
   - Error messages are linked to inputs via `aria-describedby`
   - Page title changes on route navigation

6. **Motion Preferences**:
   ```css
   @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
     *, *::before, *::after {
       animation-duration: 0.01ms !important;
       animation-iteration-count: 1 !important;
       transition-duration: 0.01ms !important;
       scroll-behavior: auto !important;
     }
   }
   ```

## Cognitive Load Minimization

### Interface Clarity
- **One primary action per screen/section**. If there are multiple CTAs, only ONE should be visually dominant.
- **Progressive disclosure**: Show essential info first, details on demand (expandable sections, modals).
- **Limit choices**: No more than 5-7 options visible at once (Miller's Law). Use search/filter for longer lists.
- **Consistent patterns**: Same action = same component = same position across all pages.

### Copy & Microcopy
- Labels should be **verbs for actions** ("Save workout", not "Submit"), **nouns for navigation** ("History", not "Go to history").
- Error messages must explain **what went wrong** AND **how to fix it**.
- Empty states must have a **call to action**, not just a description.
- **Never use technical jargon** in user-facing text (no "null", "undefined", "error 500").

### Information Architecture
- **Max 3 levels of navigation depth**. If deeper, reconsider the IA.
- **Breadcrumbs or back buttons** on any page more than 1 level deep.
- **Active navigation state** must be clearly visible — the user should always know "where am I?".

## Next.js Specific Standards

### App Router Patterns
- Use **`layout.tsx`** for shared UI (navigation, providers). Never duplicate layout across pages.
- Use **`loading.tsx`** for route-level loading states with skeleton UI.
- Use **`error.tsx`** for route-level error boundaries with user-friendly messages.
- Use **`not-found.tsx`** for custom 404 pages — never show the default.
- Use **metadata API** for SEO on every page:
  ```tsx
  export const metadata: Metadata = {
    title: 'Page Title — App Name',
    description: 'Compelling description under 160 chars',
  };
  ```

### Data Patterns
- Fetch data in **Server Components** whenever possible.
- Use **Server Actions** for mutations (form submissions, data updates).
- Client-side state only for **ephemeral UI state** (modals open, form input, animation state).
- Cache aggressively with `unstable_cache` or route segment config.

### Security
- Sanitize all user inputs.
- Use `encodeURIComponent` for URL parameters.
- Never expose API keys or secrets in client bundles.
- Use `headers()` or `cookies()` server-side, never in client components.

## Pre-Ship Checklist
- [ ] Lighthouse score ≥ 90 on Performance, Accessibility, Best Practices, SEO
- [ ] Zero axe-core violations
- [ ] Keyboard-navigable — tested Tab through entire page
- [ ] Dark mode tested — no contrast issues
- [ ] Mobile responsive — tested at 320px, 375px, 768px, 1024px, 1440px
- [ ] No layout shift on load (CLS < 0.05)
- [ ] Loading states for every async operation
- [ ] Error states for every fallible operation
- [ ] `prefers-reduced-motion` respected
- [ ] No `console.log` or `console.error` in production
